Z||000000||pherder||03-10-2000||07:39 PM||||I am in the final stages on putting a HO Quad 4 w/Isuzu 5 speed (3.88:1 FDR) into my 88 Coupe.  <P>I have been trying to get the clutch system bled with a slave cylinder that has NO bleed screw!  <P>After vacuum pumping fluid thru the system and filling the slave with fluid and then sticking the line on the slave, I end up with a clutch pedal that freely swings about 2" either side of where it rests.<P>Today I removed the stock Master Cylinder with the intentions of replacing it with a Wilwood 7/8" hydraulic master cylinder (can be used for brakes or clutch).  I was wondering how to make the pushrod work (in the Wilwood MC) so I disassembled the stock Fiero MC.  Inside was a broken spring!  The reason the clutch wouldn't work was the internal dodad (technical word for I don't have a clue what it's real word is!) could not return back to it's normal position thus the clutch pedal would swing with no resistance.<P>My next thing I do will be to see if a clutch MC rebuild kit comes with the parts I need to fix the stock Fiero's MC.  Anyone know for sure?<P>I still may need the bigger (Wilwood) master cylinder since the slave is so much bigger in diameter.  (You do remember I am putting in a transmission that never was in a Fiero?  It was in a Pontiac 97 Sunfire.)<P>Paul||||reg||4
Z||000001||william_thorniii||03-10-2000||09:42 PM||||Paul,<P>That sounds great.  I can't wait to hear the results.  Sorry, can't help you with your question though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
